    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Trigger\n\nPoint whatever marks a sale as closed at this webhook: your store, your CRM, MercadoPago, or a button in your system (**POST** with `name` and `email` in the body).\n\n*Tip:* chain it after the MercadoPago or Tiendanube template.\n\nThe webhook has no authentication and sends email. Add Header Auth before going live.",
        "height": 354,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        800
      ],
      "id": "8bb7f7c3-34dc-4b42-a4ef-1b14d443e7fb",
      "name": "Setup 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Review link and Gmail\n\n1. Get your **review link** in Google Business Profile (*Ask for reviews*, copy the `g.page/r/...` link).\n2. Replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_REVIEW_LINK` in the email.\n3. *Ask for review (email)*, Credential, connect your Gmail.\n\n*Log request* writes **name, email, asked_at**: use those headers.",
        "height": 312,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        310,
        800
      ],
      "id": "9412978e-b960-4167-beec-f994231f7440",
      "name": "Setup 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Once per customer, and variants\n\n*Ask each customer once* remembers every email it let through, across executions. The address is recorded before the send, so a failed send is not retried: asking twice annoys more than not asking.\n\n- **Wait a bit:** add a **Wait** node (for example 1 day) before the email.\n- **WhatsApp:** replace the Gmail node with an HTTP Request to the WhatsApp Cloud API, using an approved template.",
        "height": 396,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        800
      ],
      "id": "a789633a-b0c1-4da0-a621-6b1b1c31df46",
      "name": "Variants note"
    }
  ],
